    {
      "page_title": "Async, Effects and Server State",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Bug",
            "Symptom",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Race",
              "old response wins",
              "`ignore` / AbortController"
            ],
            [
              "No cleanup",
              "setState unmounted",
              "return cleanup fn"
            ],
            [
              "StrictMode",
              "fetch fires 2x",
              "cleanup makes it safe"
            ],
            [
              "No cache",
              "refetch per mount",
              "query lib / RSC"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "StrictMode is a test",
          "text": "Dev mounts, unmounts, remounts once. Effects run **twice on purpose** to surface a ==missing cleanup==. Not a bug; do not delete StrictMode."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Loading State as One Union",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// one reducer, one shape",
            "{ status: 'idle' | 'loading'",
            "        | 'success' | 'error',",
            "  data: null, error: null }"
          ],
          "note": "three useState calls allow impossible states"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`isLoading` + `data` + `error` = 8 combos, most ==illegal==",
            "Union gives 4 legal states; `switch (status)` in render",
            "Never __mirror__ props or server data into state",
            "Render from source, or from a {blue:query cache}"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Deps and Concurrent Hooks",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "What it does",
            "Use when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`useTransition`",
              "marks update **non-urgent**",
              "typing over heavy list"
            ],
            [
              "`useDeferredValue`",
              "renders ==stale== value",
              "value you don't own"
            ],
            [
              "`useOptimistic`",
              "predicts, reverts on fail",
              "like / send actions"
            ],
            [
              "Server Component",
              "fetch off client",
              "read-only data"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(fn, [{ id }])  // new ref!",
            "// runs EVERY render",
            "useEffect(fn, [id])      // fixed"
          ],
          "note": "objects compare by reference, not value"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Summary",
          "text": "Effect = sync with outside. One `{status,data,error}` union, one cleanup, primitive deps. Urgency hooks for responsiveness; ==RSC for data you only read=="
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Effects and concurrency"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Derived State, Mirrored Props and Mutation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`useEffect(()=>setFull(a+' '+b),[a,b])` — guaranteed **double render**",
            "Anything derivable during render must not pass through an effect",
            "Effect with no cleanup + StrictMode = two live requests",
            "Server Components need __no client state__ for read-only data"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Derived State",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Storing ==derived data== in state, then an effect to sync it",
            "`total` in useState + `useEffect(() => setTotal(...))`",
            "Effect runs **after** paint: one render shows stale total",
            "Fix: compute during render, `const total = items.reduce(...)`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "// bad",
            "const [full,setFull]=useState('')",
            "useEffect(()=>setFull(a+b),[a,b])",
            "// good",
            "const full = a + ' ' + b"
          ],
          "note": "no state, no effect, never stale"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Props Copied Into State",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`useState(props.user)` — later prop changes are __ignored__",
            "Initial value only reads on the **first** render",
            "Reset on identity change: `<Form key={userId} />`",
            "Never mirror server data; read the {green:query cache} directly"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Mutation and Stale Reads",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Wrong",
            "Why",
            "Right"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`items.push(x)`",
              "same ref",
              "`[...items,x]`"
            ],
            [
              "`obj.a = 1`",
              "`Object.is` true",
              "`{...obj,a:1}`"
            ],
            [
              "log after `setX`",
              "closure snapshot",
              "read in next render"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "The stale log",
          "text": "`setCount(1); console.log(count)` prints the **old** value — `count` is a const in this render's scope, not a live cell."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Redundant + Impossible State",
